      "source": "# Heads-Up Limit Texas Hold'em: Strategy & Game Theory Engine\n## Milestone 1: Stateful Engine & Hand Evaluator\n\nThis milestone builds the core of the project:\n\n1. **`Card` & `Deck`**: card representation, ordering, shuffling and dealing.\n2. **`HandEvaluator`**: picks the best 5-card hand out of 7 cards, ranks it (High Card up to Royal Flush) and breaks ties with kickers.\n3. **Monte Carlo equity engine** (Teammate 1): `calculate_equity(hole_cards, community_cards, num_simulations=10000)` plays out thousands of random boards with the `HandEvaluator` to estimate a hand's win/tie/loss percentages against a random or a specific opponent hand.\n4. **`Player`, agents & `GameEngine`**: a turn-based heads-up engine that can run on its own (AI vs. AI) or with a human seat. Betting is **No-Limit** by default (choose your size, min-raise rules, all-in); pass `betting=\"limit\"` for Fixed-Limit.\n5. **Verification & visualization**: unit tests (evaluator and equity engine), a full hand to showdown, an autonomous session and a horizontal showdown comparison chart.\n6. **Play it yourself**: run the last cell for a clickable table against the bot. The bot's cards stay face down unless the hand reaches showdown."
